- [Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/dog-beds): Before you choose between dog beds, watch how yours settles tonight. The tight curl with a nose under the tail. The chin hooked over the sofa arm. The full-length sprawl across the kitchen floor. That habit tells you more about the right bed than any photograph, and most beds here are shaped around one of them.Start with how they sleep If they curl up tight, choose walls. A dog who tucks in and presses their spine against the nearest edge tends to ignore a flat mat. Nest and donut beds give them sides all the way round. If they lean on things, choose an edge. When their chin is always resting on something, bolster beds and dog sofas put a raised, cushioned edge on one, two, three or four sides. If they sprawl, choose surface. On a walled bed their back legs end up on the floor. A dog mattress lets them step on from any side and stretch the whole length. Then decide what goes underneathFibre filling, used in nests such as Rydal and Wensleydale, is soft and yielding, but it shifts and flattens with use. Foam holds its shape under weight. Memory foam contours to the dog lying on it, and profiled egg-crate foam spreads their weight rather than compressing flat. If they have started to hesitate at the edge of the bed, look at our orthopaedic dog beds, several of which leave the front open or drop it low so there is nothing to climb. A bed is for comfort, not a treatment, so if your dog is in pain please keep talking to your vet.Size it from the sleeping areaMeasure your dog lying on their side, nose to base of tail, and add 15 to 20cm. On walled beds the sides take up part of the listed footprint: the Loweswater XL is 90 × 70cm outside but 72 × 55cm to lie on. Between two sizes, size up. If the bed is going in a crate or a car boot, measure the floor it has to lie on, not the outside of the crate.Our dog beds: the 100-night trial, and two exceptionsNo photo can tell you whether they will actually sleep on it. Your floor can. Most beds here come with a 100-night trial from delivery: if it is not right, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund (one trial per household; damage and other exclusions apply). Two exceptions. Personalised beds, such as Rydal Personalised, are made to order, so they are excluded from the trial and from change-of-mind returns, though your full legal rights apply if one arrives faulty, damaged or not as described. The Whinlatter car seat is a travel accessory, so check its returns eligibility first. Where a memory foam bed also carries a 5-year no-flatten guarantee on its foam core, its product page says so. The trial page has the full terms.Questions owners askIs UK delivery free?Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40, and every dog bed here is priced above that. Check the product page for delivery timings and any product-specific lead time before you order; our delivery and returns page covers the rest.Can I wash the covers?On most beds the cover comes off, and many wash at 30°C. Follow the sewn-in label, air-dry fully, and never wash or soak the foam. Check coated wipe-clean fabrics against their label before any machine wash, and keep Thirlmere's structured felt out of the machine.Do you have beds for very large dogs?Yes. Mardale, Longsleddale and Burnmoor are 132 × 104cm and 20cm deep, and Brotherswater's raised mesh deck is 150 × 95cm.Still not sure? The Bed Finder asks how they sleep first, then narrows the range to one bed.
- [Orthopaedic Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/orthopaedic-dog-beds): An orthopaedic dog bed earns its name in moments you have probably seen already. The two-stage stand in the morning. The hollow worn into the old bed exactly where the hips go. The stretch that takes a little longer than it used to. Some of it is age. Some of it is a surface that has packed down underneath them, and that part you can change.What makes an orthopaedic dog bed workWhether you spell it orthopaedic or orthopedic, the word should mean three physical things. First, foam that does not pack down: every bed in this collection has foam underneath rather than loose fibre (memory foam, profiled egg-crate foam, or memory foam for contour layered over egg-crate for support; Langdale and Patterdale simply list a foam base or core). Second, depth: Ennerdale is 24cm of gel memory foam, and the XXL Mardale and Longsleddale are 20cm deep. Third, a way in that does not ask for a climb. Newlands, Easedale and Burnmoor keep walls on four sides but drop the front section, and Coniston sits low with just a rim for the chin.Choosing by how they sleep and move If they lean and watch the room: three bolsters and an open front on Grasmere, Melbreak and Rosthwaite, or an L-shaped bolster with two open sides on Esthwaite and Bowfell. If they curl into a corner: Borrowdale has a border on all four sides; Skelwith closes all four around fleece; Helvellyn is a 97 × 97cm triangle that sits flush in the corner beside your sofa. If they stretch flat out: no walls at all on Buttermere (110 × 85cm, 10cm deep), Ambleside (up to 140 × 100cm) or Wastwater (127 × 91cm, with a raised head built into the foam). If they are big and heavy: Mardale, Longsleddale and Burnmoor are 132 × 104cm; Melbreak and Staveley are 122 × 89cm. Our orthopaedic buying guide takes each of these choices one step further.Liners, covers and the foam guaranteeOne accident can finish an unprotected foam core. Coniston, Borrowdale, Helvellyn, Staveley, Scafell and Newlands, among others, put a waterproof liner between the cover and the foam. Most covers come off to wash; the foam itself never should. Many of the memory foam beds here also carry a 5-year no-flatten guarantee on the foam core, subject to the guarantee terms, and the product page says when a bed does.A bed is for comfort. It is not a treatment. If your dog is in pain, recovering or finding it hard to move, keep talking to your vet about the right resting surface. If the changes you are seeing have come with age, our beds for older dogs start from there.Try it for 100 nightsWhether a bed works is something only your dog can tell you, so every orthopaedic dog bed here comes with the 100-night trial from delivery. If they do not settle on it, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund; one trial per household, and damage and other exclusions apply. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40. See how the trial works.Orthopaedic dog bed questionsWill an orthopaedic dog bed help with arthritis?It cannot treat it, and nothing here should suggest otherwise. What it changes is the surface they lie on for hours every day: foam that spreads their weight instead of bottoming out, and an entry that does not ask for a climb. Your vet is the right person for everything else.Does an orthopaedic dog bed have to be memory foam?No. Nocturne, Newlands, Easedale and Burnmoor are built on profiled egg-crate foam, which spreads weight and resists compressing flat. Martindale, Rosthwaite and Watendlath layer memory foam over egg-crate. If it is the moulding feel of memory foam you are after, our memory foam dog beds gather the beds that use it.What size orthopaedic dog bed do I need?Take their length lying on their side, nose to base of tail, then add 15 to 20cm. Bolsters sit inside the outside measurement, so if they fall between two sizes, take the bigger one.Not sure which shape suits them? The Bed Finder starts with how they sleep and narrows it to one bed.
- [Memory Foam Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/memory-foam-dog-beds): A memory foam dog bed is for the dog who circles, lies down with a heavy sigh, and an hour later gets up and shuffles, because the bed underneath has packed into ridges and the cold floor is coming through. Memory foam moulds around them as they settle and holds its shape where polyester filling packs down. Every bed here uses it, though not all in the same way.How a memory foam dog bed actually worksMemory foam contours to the dog lying on it, so a hip or shoulder settles into the surface instead of pressing on one hard spot. What differs between beds is how the foam is built: Crumb memory foam, in Chatsworth's base and Elterwater's lift-out cushion, moulds around them as they settle. Chatsworth is our lowest-priced memory foam bed. Memory foam over egg-crate foam, on Martindale, Rosthwaite, Watendlath, Skelwith, Mardale and Longsleddale: one layer to contour, one to support. Memory foam over a firmer base, on Ambleside, run right to all four edges so there is no soft rim to roll off. Gel memory foam, 24cm deep, in Ennerdale: more than twice the depth of the 10cm Buttermere mattress. Our guide to what is inside our beds sets the foams side by side.Choose the shape, then the depthFoam decides how a bed feels; shape decides whether they use it. If they sprawl: open foam. Buttermere is 110 × 85cm with nothing to climb over, and Wastwater is 127 × 91cm with a raised head built into the foam. More flat shapes are among our dog mattresses. If they lean: an arm. Grasmere and Haweswater are memory foam dog sofas, and Kendal wraps cushioned bolsters in corduroy. If they curl: walls. Borrowdale has a border on all four sides, Elterwater deep bouclé ones. If they hesitate before stepping in: Coniston keeps a chin rim but sits low. Covers, liners and the guaranteeMemory foam should never be washed or soaked, so the cover does that job, following its sewn-in label. Coniston, Borrowdale and Wastwater add a waterproof liner between cover and foam, and Elterwater a waterproof layer beneath its cover: the part that stops one bad night ending a foam bed. Most of these beds also carry a 5-year no-flatten guarantee on the foam core, subject to the guarantee terms; check the product page, which says so where it applies.Memory foam is about comfort, not treatment: if they are in pain or struggling to move, keep talking to your vet.100 nights to decideThe test is simple: does the sigh-and-shuffle stop? Every bed here except the Whinlatter car seat comes with 100 nights from delivery to find out. If it is not right, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund; one trial per household, and damage and other exclusions apply. The Whinlatter is a travel accessory, and its page says the trial should not be assumed, so check its returns eligibility before ordering. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40, and the trial page sets out the terms.Memory foam questionsIs a memory foam dog bed the same as an orthopaedic one?Often, but not always. Our orthopaedic dog beds also include profiled egg-crate builds such as Nocturne and Newlands, and the shape and height of the entry matter as much as the foam.Can a memory foam dog bed go in the washing machine?The cover can, where its label allows. The foam never should: take the cover off, wash it, air-dry it fully and refit it.How deep should a memory foam dog bed be?Deep enough that they do not reach the floor through it. Buttermere is 10cm, the XXL Mardale and Longsleddale 20cm, and Ennerdale 24cm. A heavy dog on a single thin layer is lying on your floor through a bit of fabric.Not sure which shape they need? Let the Bed Finder match a memory foam bed to how they sleep.
- [Nest & Donut Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/nest-dog-beds): A nest dog bed is for the dog who settles by curling up: a few turns, nose tucked under a back leg, spine pressed against whatever is closest, which is often the corner of your sofa. Nest and donut dog beds give them that edge all the way round, so whichever way they turn there is a wall to lean into and a soft middle to sink into.Choosing a nest or donut dog bed If they burrow out of sight: high, deep sides to get behind, on Rydal, Windermere and Elterwater. If they rest a chin on the edge: a rim rather than a wall, on Blea Tarn, Sawrey and Harewood. If they lean hard into the side: Thirlmere's walls are structured felt, so they stand up on their own instead of folding flat night after night. If they come home wet: the Crummock Waterproof Nest keeps high sides under a coated outer that wipes clean. Then pick the surface they will feel first: sherpa on Windermere and Sawrey, fleece on Rydal, velvet on Harewood, cream bouclé on Blea Tarn, and herringbone outside a lift-out inner cushion on the Crummock Herringbone Nest.Soft or supportive: what is insideMany nests are built for softness rather than support. Rydal and Wensleydale are fibre-filled and Blea Tarn soft-filled, yielding rather than firm, and that is the point: they are for sinking into. If your curler is older or stiffer, two nests here put memory foam underneath. Elterwater has a lift-out crumb memory foam cushion with a waterproof layer under the cover. Skelwith closes all four sides around memory foam over an egg-crate layer, and its foam core carries a 5-year no-flatten guarantee, subject to the guarantee terms. For firmer support across a wider choice, see our memory foam dog beds. A bed is for comfort, not a treatment; for a dog in pain, keep talking to your vet.Sizing a nest around a curled-up dogWalls eat into the footprint, so measure your dog curled up rather than stretched out, and size up if they fall between two. Sizes run from an XS at 45 × 35cm on Sawrey up to XXL on Rydal. For the smallest curlers, our small dog beds start lower still.100 nights to see if they settleSome curlers take a few nights to claim a new nest. Every nest here comes with a 100-night trial from delivery, and if they will not settle in it, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund; one trial per household, and damage and other exclusions apply. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40. Read how the trial works.Nest bed questionsWhat is the difference between a nest and a donut dog bed?Mostly the name. Both mean a raised wall all the way round a soft middle; donut usually describes a round one. Wall height and filling matter far more than the label.Are nest beds washable?Most have a zipped cover that comes off, and on Blea Tarn, Sawrey, Harewood and Wensleydale it washes at 30°C. Thirlmere's felt structure must not be machine washed, and on the Crummock Waterproof Nest, check the label first, because detergent can affect some waterproof finishes.My dog curls up but sometimes sprawls. Is a nest still right?If they stretch out as often as they curl, an edge on three sides may suit them better than four. Our bolster dog beds give them something to lean on without enclosing every side.Not sure whether yours is a nest dog? The Bed Finder asks how they sleep and tells you.
- [Bolster Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/bolster-dog-beds): A bolster dog bed is for the dog who never quite lies in the middle of anything. They wedge their back against the skirting board, rest a chin on your shoe, or lie with their spine pressed to the side of the sofa. Leaning is how they switch off, and a bolster gives that habit a place of its own: a raised, cushioned edge built into the bed.Which bolster dog bed shape suits them If they want a chin rest and room to stretch, one edge: Watendlath has a pillow bolster along one side and the rest left open. Nocturne's open-sided bolster suits big dogs who start the evening curled and end it stretched out. If they like their back covered and the room in view, two sides: Esthwaite and Bowfell have an L-shaped bolster. If they press in but find climbing hard, three sides: Melbreak, Staveley, Martindale and Rosthwaite leave the front open, so there is something to press into and nothing to climb over. Harrogate frames its cushioned base on three sides too. If they want an edge whichever way they turn, four sides: Borrowdale, Ullswater and Troutbeck. For full walls round a deep, soft middle, see our nest dog beds. Look at the sleeping area, not just the footprintA bolster is part of the bed's outside measurement, so the space they actually lie on is smaller. On the Chatsworth Large, the outside is 70 × 55cm and the sleeping area 50 × 45cm. Measure them lying down, add 15 to 20cm, and hold that number against the space inside the bolsters rather than the outside. If it is close, size up.Fibre bolsters or foam underneathKentmere, Ullswater and Loweswater are fibre-filled and Troutbeck soft-filled: yielding, made for snuggling rather than support. If they are stiffening up, choose foam under the bolsters. Chatsworth has a crumb memory foam base; Borrowdale, Melbreak and Staveley pair memory foam with a waterproof liner; Martindale and Rosthwaite layer memory foam over egg-crate foam. Langdale goes further and builds the rim itself from foam, so it holds a defined edge where a stuffed border would sag. Several of the memory foam beds here carry a 5-year no-flatten guarantee on the foam core, subject to the guarantee terms, and their product pages say so. Comfort is the job, not treatment: if your dog is in pain, keep talking to your vet.The trial on every bolster bed hereYou will only really know it is the right edge once they have used it for a while. Each one comes with 100 nights from delivery. If it turns out to be the wrong edge for them, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund; one trial per household, and damage and other exclusions apply. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40. The trial page has the detail.Bolster bed questionsIs a bolster dog bed good for older dogs?It can be, if the shape lets them walk in. Look for an open front or low entry and foam underneath; Rosthwaite and Martindale leave the front open so there is nothing to step over. Our beds for older dogs gather more.Will the bolsters go flat?Fibre-filled bolsters are soft by design, so expect some give. If a firm edge matters, choose Langdale, whose rim is foam rather than loose filling.What is the difference between a bolster bed and a dog sofa bed?Mostly shape. A sofa bed is a bolster bed built to look like furniture, usually with arms and a back. See our dog sofa beds.Torn between an edge and full walls? The Bed Finder works it out from how they sleep.
- [Dog Sofa Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/dog-sofa-beds): A dog sofa bed is for an evening routine you probably know well: curtains shut, telly on, the dog on the floor staring at you until they give up and climb onto your sofa. It is not naughtiness. Your sofa has the soft seat, the armrest and the company. A sofa bed gives them all three on a seat of their own, close enough to hear you move.Choosing a dog sofa bed by how they rest If they keep watch, head up: Haweswater has raised sofa-style sides to prop a chin on. Esthwaite and Bowfell use an L-shaped bolster along two sides, so their back is covered and the room stays in view. If they lean and flop: Grasmere has three cushioned arms and an open front, in four sizes from 80 × 60cm to 135 × 100cm. If they curl up tight: Skelwith is bolstered on all four sides around a fleece middle, at 76 × 51cm. If it has to look like furniture: Windsor is upholstered, with piped seams, furniture-weight fabric, a back and two arms, in Blue, Green, Brown or Grey. Want the arm without the furniture look? Our bolster dog beds do the same job more simply.For stiff mornings: a lower way inOften the first thing you notice is not a limp but a hesitation at the edge of the bed. Newlands, Easedale and Burnmoor keep a bolster on all four sides but drop the front section, so they step in rather than climb. Braithwaite cuts one corner open, chaise-style. These four use profiled egg-crate foam, which spreads weight rather than compressing flat, with a waterproof liner or lining around the foam for wet coats and accidents. Grasmere, Haweswater, Windsor and Skelwith use memory foam, and their foam cores carry a 5-year no-flatten guarantee, subject to the guarantee terms. For more low-entry shapes, see our orthopaedic dog beds. A sofa bed is about comfort, not treatment; for pain or stiffness, keep talking to your vet.Sizes from small dogs to giantsBraithwaite, Skelwith and Newlands suit small and medium dogs. For big dogs, Easedale and Scafell are 106.5 × 81.5cm, Bowfell 122 × 91cm, and Burnmoor 132 × 104cm and 20cm deep. The arms sit inside the outside footprint, so check the seat they will actually lie on against their length lying flat, plus 15 to 20cm. Between sizes, go up.100 nights on a seat of their ownEvery sofa bed here is covered by the 100-night trial from delivery. If they still prefer your sofa after a fair try, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund, with one trial per household and damage and other exclusions applying. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40. The trial in full.Dog sofa bed questionsWill my dog stay off my sofa if they have their own?Nobody can honestly promise that. What a sofa bed does is offer the same three things, an arm, a soft seat and a view of you, so they have a good reason to stay on theirs. Haweswater and Grasmere are both sized to sit right beside your chair.Can I wash a dog sofa bed?On most of these the cover comes off; wash it following the sewn-in label and never wash or soak the foam. Where there is a liner, wipe it, then let everything air-dry fully before refitting.Which dog sofa bed is easiest to get into?The ones with a lowered front, Newlands, Easedale and Burnmoor, or Grasmere, whose open front has nothing to step over at all.Not sure which of these suits them? The Bed Finder decides from how they sleep.
- [Dog Mattresses & Flat Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/dog-mattresses): A dog mattress is for the sprawler: the dog who lies flat on their side, legs out, diagonally across the rug, and on a walled bed ends up with back legs on the floor and head jammed into a corner. Take the walls away and nearly every centimetre is somewhere they can lie, and they can step on from any side, at any age.Which dog mattress for which dog If they are a big side sleeper who needs support: memory foam. Buttermere is 110 × 85cm and 10cm deep. Ambleside layers memory foam over a firmer base right to all four edges, up to 140 × 100cm. Wastwater is 127 × 91cm with a raised head built into the foam. If they want soft: Hawkshead (faux fur) and Seathwaite (sherpa) are open pillow mattresses filled with virgin fibre, 100 × 65cm or 120 × 80cm and 20cm deep, with leather handles to carry them to wherever the warm spot is tonight. If they want fur on top and foam below: Patterdale puts a faux-fur sleeping surface over a foam core, in brown herringbone tweed. If they curl one night and sprawl the next: Duddon is an 80 × 80cm square for dogs who sleep diagonally, teddy fleece on one face and canvas on the other. If it is for a crate or wet walks: Glenridding is a quilted crate mattress with low padded sides; Wasdale's green outer fabric is itself the waterproof layer. Runs hot, or always ends up on the tiles? A raised mesh deck may suit them better than any mattress: see our elevated and cooling dog beds.What decides whether a flat bed lastsA mattress has nowhere to hide a thin spot. On a thin foam sheet a dog lying near the edge sinks through to the floor and shuffles back to the middle. Foam that runs edge to edge, or two layers doing different jobs, is what stops that. Buttermere, Ambleside and Wastwater also carry a 5-year no-flatten guarantee on the foam core, subject to the guarantee terms. Fibre mattresses are deliberately softer; choose them for comfort rather than support. For a dog in pain or recovering, keep talking to your vet about the right resting surface.Measuring for a mattressEasier than for any other bed. Measure your dog lying on their side, nose to base of tail, and add 15 to 20cm. Most of these have no bolsters to allow for, so the listed size is close to the size they get. For a crate, measure the inside of the crate base and choose the size that lies flat without bunching or blocking the door.100 nights to stretch out on itWhether they use the whole surface is easy to see once it is down, and you have plenty of time to watch. Every mattress here comes with a 100-night trial from delivery. If it is not right, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund (one trial per household; damage and other exclusions apply). Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40. The trial page explains how it works.Dog mattress questionsIs a flat dog mattress a good choice for an older dog?It removes the climb, which matters for a stiff dog. Choose foam rather than fibre if they need support, and see our orthopaedic dog beds for more shapes with low or open entries.Can a dog mattress go in a crate?Yes, if it lies flat. Glenridding comes in 70 × 50cm, 90 × 60cm and 105 × 70cm to compare with your crate base. Our crate and travel beds include wipe-clean options.How do I wash a dog mattress?Unzip the cover and follow its sewn-in label (several wash at 30°C), and keep the foam out of the machine. Wasdale's waterproof outer is wiped for everyday marks; check the label before washing its covers.Not sure you have a sprawler? The Bed Finder starts from how they sleep and suggests one bed.
- [Elevated & Cooling Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/elevated-cooling-dog-beds): An elevated dog bed is for the dog who seeks out the coolest floor in the house: flat out on the kitchen tiles in summer, sprawled across the utility room flagstones, moving to a fresh patch when the old one warms up. A raised frame with a taut mesh deck gives them a surface with air on both sides. That is the whole idea behind the mesh beds here: no gel, no batteries, nothing inside to leak or run flat.How an elevated or cooling dog bed worksOn a solid bed or a floor, warmth builds up between the dog and the surface. Lift the deck clear and air moves underneath, so warm air moves away instead of collecting beneath them. The mesh is pulled taut, so it takes their weight evenly across the deck. The same lift helps in winter: on cold tiles or a damp utility floor, a raised deck keeps them off the coldest surface in the house, with a blanket laid on top. One honest limit: a raised bed, canopy or kennel does not prevent overheating. In hot weather they still need drinking water, safe shade, and to come indoors in extreme heat.Choosing between the frames If they sprawl and come home muddy: Bassenthwaite, a metal frame and breathable mesh at 90 × 70cm, 110 × 80cm or 130 × 90cm, with no foam or filling to go soggy after a wet walk. Rinse it down and let it dry. If they sprawl and you want it all year: Windermere, a steel frame and taut mesh deck at the same three footprints. Lay a blanket on top for the cold months and take it off when the heat comes back. There is no cover to unzip. If they lean: Brotherswater, with bolsters on three sides around a 150 × 95cm deck, a powder-coated steel frame, non-slip rubber feet and snap-together assembly with no tools. If you want a lounger for the patio: Henley and Torver are woven day beds with a canopy and an included cushion, for supervised lounging on a patio or in a conservatory. They are not all-weather shelter; for kennels with raised floors, see our outdoor dog houses. Who they suitHot sleepers, thick-coated breeds, muddy dogs and homes with hard floors. A taut mesh deck feels firm, so a dog who likes to sink into something soft may prefer it with a blanket on top, or a soft dog mattress instead. For size, go by their length lying on their side plus 15 to 20cm, as you would for any flat bed.Trial and returns: two sets of terms hereWindermere, Bassenthwaite and Brotherswater come with the 100-night trial from delivery, long enough to see how they use it as the weather changes: if it is not right, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund (one trial per household; damage and other exclusions apply). Henley and Torver are outdoor day beds, so they have a 30-day change-of-mind window, with return at your cost, not the 100-night sleep trial. Your statutory rights are unaffected. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40. Delivery and returns in full.Elevated dog bed questionsDoes a cooling dog bed stop a dog overheating?No bed can promise that. A raised mesh deck lets air move underneath so heat does not build up beneath them, but on hot days they still need water, shade and, in extreme heat, to come inside.Can an elevated dog bed go outside?Windermere, Bassenthwaite and Brotherswater are made for the garden in summer as well as indoors, and Bassenthwaite can simply be rinsed down. Henley and Torver are for supervised lounging in suitable weather; store their cushions under cover.How do I clean a raised mesh bed?Wipe or rinse the mesh and frame and let it dry fully. Keep it on a level surface and check the frame joints occasionally.Not sure a raised bed suits how they sleep? The Bed Finder will point you to one bed.
- [Waterproof Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/waterproof-dog-beds): A waterproof dog bed is for the walk that ends the same way every time: a soaked dog through the door, a quick go with the towel, and straight onto their bed before you can stop them. On fleece or plush, that means a damp bed, a wash cycle and a day of drying. On a coated outer, it means a damp cloth, and the bed is back in use.Outer coating or inner liner: two kinds of waterproof dog bedThe beds in this collection deal with mess on the outside. Wasdale's green outer fabric is itself the waterproof layer, and the Crummock Waterproof Nest, Ribble and Derwent have coated, wipe-clean outers, so mud, drool and wet paws stay on the surface and come off with a cloth. That is different from a waterproof inner liner, which sits hidden between a washable cover and the foam to protect the core from accidents. If foam support matters more than a wipe-clean surface, beds such as Coniston, Borrowdale and Scafell have liners inside; you will find them among our orthopaedic dog beds.Choosing by how they sleep, and where If they sprawl: Wasdale has no raised sides, a filled support layer, leather handles and a non-slip base, at 75 × 55cm or 95 × 75cm. If they curl: the Crummock Waterproof Nest keeps high walls on every side over a cushioned base, at 65 × 45cm, 70 × 55cm or 90 × 70cm. It is a nest, not a firm foam mattress. If they lean, in a crate: Ribble puts bolstered sides into a crate-shaped bed, in four sizes from 70 × 55cm to 105 × 75cm. If it is for the boot or a crate floor: Derwent is a low-profile mat at 60 × 45cm, 75 × 55cm or 90 × 65cm. Looking after a coated bedWipe the outer for everyday marks; Derwent wipes down with a damp cloth and mild soap. Before you machine-wash any removable cover, check the sewn-in label, because detergent and machine washing can affect some waterproof finishes, and do not machine-wash Derwent unless its label expressly permits it. Let everything dry before it goes back down. Our care guide has the full routine. In the car, a bed is a comfort accessory, not a vehicle restraint, so use a proper restraint as well.Give it a wet season: the 100-night trialEvery bed here comes with the 100-night trial from delivery, and should it not suit them, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund, one trial per household, with damage and other exclusions applying. Standard UK delivery is free on orders over £40.Waterproof dog bed questionsIs a waterproof dog bed a good idea for a puppy or an older dog?The Crummock Waterproof Nest is made for curled-up sleepers with muddy hobbies, puppies, and older dogs who have the occasional accident: everyday marks wipe off between proper washes. For a foam bed protected from the inside, choose one with a waterproof liner. If accidents are new for an older dog, mention them to your vet.Can I machine wash a waterproof dog bed?Check the label first. Some covers can be washed, but detergent and machine washing can affect waterproof finishes, so wiping is the everyday routine. If you would rather wash than wipe, see our washable dog beds.Which one works in a crate?Ribble and Derwent, measured against the inside of the crate base so they lie flat without bunching or blocking the door. Our crate and travel beds include a quilted option too.Not sure which suits them? The Bed Finder picks one bed from how they sleep.
- [Crate & Travel Dog Beds](https://pawlunova.co.uk/collections/crate-travel-dog-beds): The crate is often the most-used bed in the house: the whole night, the school run, the hour you're out. A bare tray is cold, hard and loud every time they shift, and a folded blanket ends up in one corner by morning. A dog crate bed is cut to lie flat in that space, so the padding stays under them instead of bunched against the bars.Dog crate beds, mats and a car seatFour pieces, each doing a slightly different job: Glenridding: a quilted crate mattress with low padded sides and a zipped cover that washes at 30°C. Small 70 × 50cm, Medium 90 × 60cm, Large 105 × 70cm. Ribble: bolstered sides to lean on, a padded middle and a coated outer that wipes clean after a wet walk. Four sizes, 70 × 55cm to 105 × 75cm. Derwent: a low-profile mat with a coated, wipe-clean surface, in three footprints from 60 × 45cm to 90 × 65cm. Whinlatter: a car seat with around 10cm of memory foam, an inside listed at about 66 × 38cm and a stated limit of about 25kg. How to choose: crate, boot or back seatStart with the space, not the dog. Measure the inside of the crate base or the boot floor, then choose the size that lies flat without bunching or blocking the door. A bed that rides up at the edges gives them a ridge to lie on. Then match it to how they rest: If they prop their chin on things: Ribble's bolsters or Glenridding's low padded edge. If they drop and sleep, or come back from every walk soaked: Derwent's flat, wipeable surface. If they ride on the seat rather than in the boot: Whinlatter, checked against its listed inside size and load before you order. What makes a crate bed workFit and surface. It has to reach the edges so the whole floor is padded, and its surface has to survive the drive home from a muddy field. Ribble and Derwent use coated fabric you wipe down; Glenridding's cover unzips for the machine. Check the sewn-in label before washing any coated cover, because detergent can affect some waterproof finishes. For a flat bed for the rest of the house, see our dog mattresses.And one plain safety line: a bed is a comfort accessory, not a vehicle restraint. Whinlatter is not crash-tested safety equipment, so use a suitable restraint and follow the fitting instructions.Trying it at homeA crate bed has to earn its place over a few weeks of nights and journeys. Glenridding, Ribble and Derwent come with the 100-night sleep trial: if it isn't right within 100 nights, we arrange free UK mainland collection and a full refund. One trial per household; damage and other exclusions apply. Whinlatter is a travel accessory, so check its returns terms before ordering rather than assuming the trial covers it. Free standard UK delivery on orders over £40.Crate bed questionsWhat size dog crate bed do I need?Measure the inside of the crate base, length and width, and choose the size that matches without folding. If you're torn between two, the one that lies flat beats the one that buckles. The size guide shows how to measure your dog too.Can I use a crate bed in the car?Yes, as somewhere comfortable to lie in the boot or a travel crate, alongside a proper restraint. Ribble and Derwent both come in sizes to measure against a boot floor.Are these crate beds waterproof?Ribble and Derwent have coated, wipe-clean outers, which handle wet paws and mud between washes. Of the beds in our waterproof dog beds, Wasdale and the Crummock Waterproof Nest are the ones whose fabric is described as waterproof.Not sure which fits your dog's routine? The Bed Finder asks how they sleep and points you to one bed.
